Coatings for semiconductor equipment parts protect chamber components, shields, liners, rings, and other precision parts exposed to plasma, reactive gases, high temperatures, and repeated cleaning cycles. These protective layers help reduce corrosion, erosion, particle generation, and contamination that could affect wafer quality and manufacturing yields.

As semiconductor fabrication advances toward more complex device structures and increasingly demanding process recipes, equipment operators require coatings that maintain surface integrity over extended operating periods. Ceramic coatings, particularly yttria- and alumina-based systems, are important in plasma-facing applications, while metallic and alloy coatings address selected wear, thermal-management, and mechanical requirements.

